SplitMind patch 0020 for OpenConnector v1.9.2.
Upstream issue: not filed yet. Draft text: docs/upstream/connection-read-only-issue-draft.md, section "Mislabelled actions" (#134, the pass-through audit).
Replace this line with the upstream issue or pull request link once it exists.

From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Feder <noreply@splitmind.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:10:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(catalog): label pass-through and mutating actions as
 write or destructive

Read-only connections (0018) and the read-only MCP consent grants (0004)
trust each action's operationType. The #134 audit found actions labelled
read that forward caller-chosen tools, SQL, GraphQL, code or HTTP methods,
or that plainly mutate:

- destructive: google_bigquery.query (raw GoogleSQL runs DML and DDL; the
  required scopes are unchanged) and okta.lifecycle_user (deactivates and
  suspends users).
- write: gildata.call_tool, pkulaw.call_tool, investoday_mcp.call_tool,
  finchina.execute_tool, sif.call_tool, tongdaxin.call_tool,
  fireflies.execute_graphql_query (its read-only guard has a bypass,
  reported privately upstream), waffo.run_query, wandb.query_wandb,
  turbot_pipes.execute_query, vapi.test_code_tool_execution,
  scrapfly.scrape, scrapingant.scrape_with_extended_json_output,
  scrapingant.extract_content_as_markdown and
  scrapingant.extract_data_with_ai.

Descriptions that claimed read-only (tongdaxin, fireflies, waffo, wandb) no
longer do. Actions that gate on an allowlist (baizhi_mcp, helium10) and the
public scrape OpenAPI invokers stay read.
